<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Julu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">207 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Julu was fought in 207 BCE near Julu, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebei">Hebei</a>, between rebel forces led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> armies besieging the city. Xiang Yu crossed the river, had his boats sunk and cooking pots broken so his men could not retreat, and defeated the Qin generals in a series of engagements. The victory destroyed Qin's main field army and made Xiang Yu the leading rebel commander.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-julu.jpg" alt="Battle of Julu" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vitsuha · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%B7%A8%E9%B9%BF%E4%B9%8B%E6%88%B0_%E9%82%A2%E5%8F%B0%E5%8D%9A%E7%89%A9%E9%A4%A8.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
